🌳 LeetCode 100 — Same Tree
1. Problem Statement

You are given the roots of two binary trees p and q.

You need to check whether the two trees are exactly the same.

Two trees are considered the same if:

Their corresponding nodes have the same values.
Their structures are the same.

Example:

Tree 1:        1
              / \
             2   3

Tree 2:        1
              / \
             2   3

Answer:

true

But:

Tree 1:        1
              /
             2

Tree 2:        1
                \
                 2

Answer:

false

Even though the values are the same, their structures are different.


Logic :

I compare the two trees recursively.
If both nodes are null, they are equal at that position. 
If only one is null, the structures are different, so I return false.
Otherwise, I check whether their values are equal and recursively compare their left and right subtrees.
All three conditions must be true for the two trees to be identical

Code :

public boolean isSameTree(TreeNode p, TreeNode q) {
        if(p==null && q==null){
            return true;
        }
        if(p==null || q==null){
            return false;
        }
        return p.val==q.val && isSameTree(p.left,q.left) && isSameTree(p.right,q.right);
    }
